WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.839
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Writing Skills.

2
00:00:05.139 --> 00:00:08.433
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.733 --> 00:00:13.719
Unit seven: Formal Letters. Today you will write a formal letter with the correct layout.

4
00:00:14.019 --> 00:00:16.555
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:20.733
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:21.583 --> 00:00:22.329
Formal.

7
00:00:23.317 --> 00:00:25.966
Formal means serious and correct in style.

8
00:00:26.550 --> 00:00:28.259
Use a formal style.

9
00:00:28.850 --> 00:00:31.305
Your turn. Say: Formal.

10
00:00:34.167 --> 00:00:35.017
Formal.

11
00:00:35.783 --> 00:00:36.784
Applicant.

12
00:00:37.783 --> 00:00:40.491
Applicant means a person who applies for something.

13
00:00:41.083 --> 00:00:42.839
The applicant sent a letter.

14
00:00:43.450 --> 00:00:45.800
Your turn. Say: Applicant.

15
00:00:48.667 --> 00:00:49.656
Applicant.

16
00:00:50.417 --> 00:00:51.476
Enclose.

17
00:00:52.483 --> 00:00:55.156
Enclose means to put something inside with a letter.

18
00:00:55.750 --> 00:00:57.517
I enclose my certificate.

19
00:00:58.117 --> 00:01:00.990
Your turn. Say: Enclose.

20
00:01:03.833 --> 00:01:05.508
Enclose.

21
00:01:06.250 --> 00:01:07.332
Sincerely.

22
00:01:08.317 --> 00:01:11.048
Sincerely means a formal way to end a letter.

23
00:01:11.650 --> 00:01:13.673
Yours sincerely, Dara Kem.

24
00:01:14.283 --> 00:01:16.750
Your turn. Say: Sincerely.

25
00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:20.729
Sincerely.

26
00:01:21.483 --> 00:01:22.496
Recipient.

27
00:01:23.483 --> 00:01:25.994
Recipient means the person who gets a letter.

28
00:01:26.583 --> 00:01:28.293
Write the recipient's address.

29
00:01:28.883 --> 00:01:31.443
Your turn. Say: Recipient.

30
00:01:34.300 --> 00:01:35.498
Recipient.

31
00:01:36.250 --> 00:01:37.135
Complaint.

32
00:01:38.150 --> 00:01:40.405
Complaint means saying that something is wrong.

33
00:01:41.017 --> 00:01:42.830
I am writing to make a complaint.

34
00:01:43.417 --> 00:01:46.011
Your turn. Say: Complaint.

35
00:01:48.867 --> 00:01:49.798
Complaint.

36
00:01:50.550 --> 00:01:51.470
Enquire.

37
00:01:52.483 --> 00:01:54.727
Enquire means to ask for information.

38
00:01:55.317 --> 00:01:57.688
I am writing to enquire about a course.

39
00:01:58.283 --> 00:02:01.087
Your turn. Say: Enquire.

40
00:02:03.933 --> 00:02:05.027
Enquire.

41
00:02:05.783 --> 00:02:07.028
Opportunity.

42
00:02:08.017 --> 00:02:10.620
Opportunity means a chance to do something.

43
00:02:11.217 --> 00:02:12.949
Thank you for the opportunity.

44
00:02:13.550 --> 00:02:16.725
Your turn. Say: Opportunity.

45
00:02:19.567 --> 00:02:20.707
Opportunity.

46
00:02:21.500 --> 00:02:25.244
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:26.083 --> 00:02:28.629
Visal, how do I start a formal letter?

48
00:02:29.717 --> 00:02:38.058
Write your address, the date and the recipient's address. Start with Dear Sir or Madam, or Dear Mr Chan if you know the name.

49
00:02:39.150 --> 00:02:40.871
What is the first sentence?

50
00:02:41.983 --> 00:02:48.386
Say your purpose clearly. For example, I am writing to enquire about your English course.

51
00:02:49.483 --> 00:02:50.740
How do I finish?

52
00:02:51.850 --> 00:02:59.437
Use Yours faithfully with Dear Sir or Madam, and Yours sincerely with a name. Then sign and print your name.

53
00:03:00.600 --> 00:03:02.251
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:03.117 --> 00:03:05.732
Grammar focus: Purpose of the letter.

55
00:03:06.032 --> 00:03:07.184
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:07.883 --> 00:03:10.707
I am writing to enquire about your English course.

57
00:03:11.617 --> 00:03:14.464
I am writing to apply for the position of teacher.

58
00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:20.212
Open a formal letter with I am writing to plus a verb. Do not use contractions.

59
00:03:20.950 --> 00:03:24.334
Be careful! Don't say: I am writing for ask about it.

60
00:03:26.300 --> 00:03:28.590
Say: I am writing to ask about it.

61
00:03:28.890 --> 00:03:30.460
Use to plus verb.

62
00:03:31.267 --> 00:03:33.815
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:34.600 --> 00:03:36.031
A Letter of Enquiry.

64
00:03:36.331 --> 00:03:38.922
Vireak wants to join an English course.

65
00:03:39.933 --> 00:03:42.142
He writes a formal letter to the school.

66
00:03:43.133 --> 00:03:45.168
He begins with Dear Sir or Madam.

67
00:03:46.167 --> 00:03:49.408
He writes, I am writing to enquire about your evening classes.

68
00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:53.096
He ends with Yours faithfully and signs his name.

69
00:03:54.200 --> 00:03:58.109
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:03:58.950 --> 00:04:01.112
A formal letter does not use blank.

71
00:04:01.412 --> 00:04:05.205
A, dates. B, contractions. C, words.

72
00:04:08.767 --> 00:04:11.219
The answer is B: contractions.

73
00:04:12.383 --> 00:04:14.812
Dear Sir or Madam ends with Yours blank.

74
00:04:15.112 --> 00:04:18.975
A, sincerely. B, soon. C, faithfully.

75
00:04:22.533 --> 00:04:24.765
The answer is C: faithfully.

76
00:04:25.917 --> 00:04:27.696
Enquire means to blank.

77
00:04:27.996 --> 00:04:31.254
A, ask. B, pay. C, hide.

78
00:04:34.800 --> 00:04:36.765
The answer is A: ask.

79
00:04:37.917 --> 00:04:40.102
Enclose means to put blank inside.

80
00:04:40.402 --> 00:04:43.672
A, water. B, something. C, nothing.

81
00:04:47.233 --> 00:04:49.175
The answer is B: something.

82
00:04:50.317 --> 00:04:52.374
Vireak writes about evening blank.

83
00:04:52.674 --> 00:04:56.188
A, food. B, trips. C, classes.

84
00:04:59.733 --> 00:05:01.942
The answer is C: classes.

85
00:05:03.133 --> 00:05:06.204
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:07.050 --> 00:05:08.794
How do you write a formal letter?

87
00:05:17.583 --> 00:05:18.944
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:19.244 --> 00:05:30.305
I write the addresses and the date, then start with Dear Sir or Madam. I state my purpose with I am writing to. I avoid contractions and end with Yours faithfully.

89
00:05:30.605 --> 00:05:32.454
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:33.350 --> 00:05:37.256
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and purpose of the letter.

91
00:05:37.556 --> 00:05:42.670
Today's value is professionalism. Be prepared, polite and reliable in everything you do.

92
00:05:42.970 --> 00:05:45.436
See you in Unit eight. Goodbye!

93
00:05:45.736 --> 00:05:48.099
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

